  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), the page state: AQ listing (`getAlertesByTopic`) and AQ RSS feed, with HTML entities in titles, authors and comments\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: AQ listing (`getAlertesByTopic`) and AQ RSS feed, with HTML entities in titles, authors and comments\n\nNote: third-party host `aq.super-h.fr` (LOT-001 (#38) checklist row P08, skipped while Q-4 was open); Q-4 is decided (keep, first-use notice), so capture it now, plus a legacy oracle for the parser\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field; never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36); add a legacy oracle when a parser consumes it (LOT-002 (#39)..005 tooling); one PR per batch of captures; the PR removes the row from the Capture backlog.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-028 (#56), LOT-055 (#81), BUG-4 (#105)\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (ready; `host: mac`)\n\n### Source\n\n`docs/LOTS.md` \"Capture backlog (Mac)\", copied from the frozen old issue [francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#98](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/issues/98).\n",
